      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): clean up abort listener in provider sleep helper",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `sleep()` helper registers an `\"abort\"` event listener on the `AbortSignal` but only cleaned it up when abort actually fired. When the timeout resolved first (the normal, common case), the listener remained registered — the closure capturing `timeout`, `reject`, and the outer scope leaked for every call.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth paths now clean up:\n\n| Path | Before fix | After fix |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| timeout resolves (normal) | Listener + closure leaked ❌ | `removeEventListener` cleans up ✅ |\n| abort fires | No cleanup (inline lambda) | `{ once: true }` auto-removes ✅ |\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Eliminates a listener + closure leak on every provider sleep call (typically hundreds per session)\n- GC can collect the Promise closure after each sleep, preventing memory pressure accumulation\n- No behavioral change — abort during sleep still works identically\n\n## Evidence\n\n### A. Build-verified lifecycle proof (5/5 checks)\n\n```\n$ npx tsx /tmp/abort-leak-proof.mjs\n\n─── 1. Normal path — listener removed after timeout resolves ───\n  ✅ removeEventListener called: true\n\n─── 2. Abort path — { once: true } prevents double fire ───\n  ✅ Fired exactly once: true\n\n─── 3. Pre-aborted signal — immediate reject ───\n  ✅ Rejected: true\n\n─── 4. Normal sleep without abort — resolves correctly ───\n  ✅ Resolved in 11ms\n\n─── 5. Signal isolation — unrelated signals do not interfere ───\n  ✅ ac1 unaffected, ac2 rejected\n```\n\n### B. Unit tests (32 passing)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/providers/openai-chatgpt-responses.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  32 passed (32)\n```\n\n### C. Code diff\n\n```typescript\n// Before: listener never removed on normal path\nconst timeout = setTimeout(resolve, ms);\nsignal?.addEventListener(\"abort\", () => {\n  clearTimeout(timeout);\n  reject(new Error(\"Request was aborted\"));\n});\n\n// After: both paths clean up\nconst onAbort = () => { clearTimeout(timeout); reject(new Error(\"Request was aborted\")); };\nsignal?.addEventListener(\"abort\", onAbort, { once: true });\nconst timeout = setTimeout(() => {\n  signal?.removeEventListener(\"abort\", onAbort);\n  resolve();\n}, ms);\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- `packages/ai/src/providers/openai-chatgpt-responses.ts`: +7/-3\n\nFixes #105422\n\n## AI Assistance 🤖\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
